@note +1 kind=security risk=high confidence=0.8 id=security
urgency: urgent
why: Validate the new value at the boundary because downstream consumers assume it is trusted.
source: inference — fixture only
verify: none

@note +1 kind=intent confidence=0.7 id=intent
urgency: normal
why: Keep the descriptive value so callers can inspect its purpose before using it.
verify: none

@note +1..2 kind=test id=overlap
why: The same value has a second consumer, so the regression needs both call paths.
verify: none

@note -1 kind=security id=old-security
why: The removed value was previously treated as trusted without validation.
verify: none

@note +3 kind=note id=last
why: Preserve the separate third case so adjacent comment layout remains readable.
verify: none

